.TH geectl-local-build-build 1  "geectl-local-build-build 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-local\-build\-build \- Build the package in the container: the run\-mode service run, the precommit gate, then the engine build
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl local\-build build\fR [\fB\-\-arch\fR] [\fB\-\-flavor\fR] [\fB\-\-clean\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-trust\-all\-projects\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-image\fR] [\fB\-\-alternative\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-noinit\fR] [\fB\-\-preinstall\-image\fR] [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-keep\-rpms\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-prefer\-packages\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-repo\fR> <\fIDIRECTORY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build the package in the container: the run\-mode service run, the precommit gate, then the engine build.
.PP
A failing pre\-step fails the command before the build runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The OBS project the package belongs to
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
The repository to build for (e.g. `standard`)
.TP
\fB\-\-arch\fR \fI<ARCH>\fR
The architecture to build for; must equal the host arch
.TP
\fB\-\-flavor\fR \fI<FLAVOR>\fR
The multibuild flavor; required when the source carries a `_multibuild` file. One invocation builds one flavor
.TP
\fB\-\-clean\fR
Wipe the root before building
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR
The release number, passed through to the engine
.TP
\fB\-\-trust\-all\-projects\fR
Allow build dependencies from other users\*(Aq `home:` projects (their packages run code in the build root). Without this such builds are refused
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-image\fR
Force an image pull even when the local image is fresh
.TP
\fB\-\-alternative\-project\fR \fI<ALTERNATIVE_PROJECT>\fR
Build against another project instead of `project`: buildinfo, buildconfig, the trust check, and dep resolution use it. The root stays keyed by `project`
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
Build in this directory instead of the derived cache\-dir root
.TP
\fB\-\-noinit\fR
Skip the root initialization: start the build immediately in the existing root. Needs an initialized root (a previous build wrote the rpmlist and buildconfig there)
.TP
\fB\-\-preinstall\-image\fR
Use the preinstall image when the buildinfo offers one. Off by default: the engine extracts the image with bsdtar `\-\-chroot` plus device nodes, which need root. The engine always runs as container root, so the image is always selectable
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\-rpms\fR \fI<KEEP_RPMS>\fR
Save the built RPMs into this directory (created when missing) on a green build
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-prefer\-packages\fR \fI<PREFER_PACKAGES>\fR
Prefer RPMs from this directory when installing the build root: a dep whose file is there is used instead of the cached or downloaded copy
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR \fI<TIMEOUT_SECS>\fR [default: 3600]
Timeout in seconds for the whole run
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIDIRECTORY\fR>
The source directory (spec + sources)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
